18:01:03Z","closed_at":"2019-06-03T00:15:04Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":"resolved","sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Hi, thanks for the great form library.\r\nI'm trying version 3.8.6 with typescript, but `errors` type completion doesn't work well. \r\n\r\nDemo\r\n```ts\r\ntype FormData = {\r\n  name: string;\r\n};\r\n\r\nconst App: React.FC<SomeProps> = props => {\r\n  const defaultValues: FormData = {\r\n    name: props.name\r\n  };\r\n  const { register, handleSubmit, errors } = useForm<FormData>({\r\n    mode: \"onSubmit\",\r\n    defaultValues,\r\n  });\r\n\r\n  return (\r\n    <form onSubmit={handleSubmit(data => console.log(data))}>\r\n      <input\r\n        name=\"name\"\r\n        ref={register({ required: \"name is required.\" })}\r\n      />\r\n      {errors.name && errors.name.message}\r\n      // Property 'name' does not exist on type 'typeof' ErrorMessages<FormData>\r\n\r\n      <input type=\"submit\" />\r\n    </form>\r\n  );\r\n};\r\n```\r\n\r\nI read the source code and think this line is the cause.\r\nhttps://github.com/bluebill1049/react-hook-form/blob/97952827cb90e145622e9f3c28087e91c3ff9f95/src/types.ts#L61\r\n\r\nDo you think `| {}` is needed? Or, I'm glad you tell me the workaround.","closed_by":{"login":"bluebill1049","id":10513364,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwNTEzMzY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10513364?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluebill1049","html_url":"https://github.com/bluebill1049","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluebill1049/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluebill1049/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluebill1049/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bluebill1049/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":